Z||000000||longjonsilver||11-24-2001||05:03 PM||||been poking around the wrecking yards and noticed that the airboxes contain baffles- this is leaving me baffled!  wouldnt it be better to remove them so that the airflow is unobstructed to the snorkel?<BR><P>------------------<BR>au revoir||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||11-24-2001||06:27 PM||||Well, the airbox has shown that it isn't terribly restrictive for what the 2.8 motor (in stock form) wants. You won't see much difference going to a custom intake without a dyno... even then, not much... + 1-2HP, - 1-2Ftlbs... It's a trade off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The baffles are there to stop water from shooting into the intake when you go over puddles. I'm cutting mine out, since it makes nifty sucking noises  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000002||theogre||11-25-2001||03:07 PM||||The air box serves a dual purpose of keeping out large amounts of water and reducing noise. In terms of air flow, it's been tested and found not to be a problem. Somewhere a long time ago I remember someone even dyno'd a few differant intakes and found little or no dif. I seem to recall one of them actually hurt performance some.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||11-26-2001||08:17 PM||||I turned the fenderwell into my airbox,made a baffle behind the grill aways to keep water off of my K&N that's up in there.<BR>But unless you really have some airflow,it won't do much;my 3.4,four valve/cyl. V6 ran pretty darn good sucking through the stock airbox,with baffle.||||reg||1
